# Strong's pipeline — what ships vs what is reproducible.
#
# data/ IS committed: Pages serves it, so the app needs it in the repo.
# These are the inputs and intermediates that produced it, and nothing
# fetches them at runtime.

# The monoliths. Superseded by data/ — kept locally as the inputs to
# split_for_phone.py, but 15MB of dead weight in a Pages deploy.
/bible-tagged.json
/strongs-lexicon.json

# 40MB of upstream source blobs. NOTES.md §5 has the exact commands to
# refetch both from GitHub. em_q_strongs_pipeline/output/ stays tracked, so
# the split can be re-run without them.
em_q_strongs_pipeline/sources/
